## Cypher cookbook

Direct queries for the Neo4j Browser or your own driver code, when the Python helpers above don't cover what you need. All read-only unless marked otherwise.

**Get a user's assigned track**
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})-[:ASSIGNED_TO]->(t:Track)
RETURN t.track_id, t.name
```

**Get a user's most recent N sessions**
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})-[:HAS_SESSION]->(s:Session)
RETURN s.session_id, s.overall_score, s.speech_rate_wpm, s.filler_total, s.timestamp
ORDER BY s.timestamp DESC
LIMIT $n
```

**Get every phoneme score for one session**
```cypher
MATCH (s:Session {session_id: $session_id})-[:CONTAINS_SCORE]->(sc:Score)-[:FOR_PHONEME]->(p:Phoneme)
RETURN p.symbol, sc.value
```

**Get a user's average score per phoneme, across all sessions**
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})-[:HAS_SESSION]->(:Session)-[:CONTAINS_SCORE]->(sc:Score)-[:FOR_PHONEME]->(p:Phoneme)
RETURN p.symbol, avg(sc.value) AS avg_score
ORDER BY avg_score ASC
```

**Get a user's current weak phonemes** (same as `WEAK_AT` edges, computed live instead of relying on `update_weak_phonemes()` having been run recently)
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})-[:WEAK_AT]->(p:Phoneme)
RETURN p.symbol
```

**Get a user's total session count and first/last session timestamp** (useful for streaks / consistency checks)
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})-[:HAS_SESSION]->(s:Session)
RETURN count(s) AS session_count, min(s.timestamp) AS first_session, max(s.timestamp) AS last_session
```

**Get every session that's missing an embedding** (find sessions DTW comparison will skip)
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})-[:HAS_SESSION]->(s:Session)
WHERE s.embedding IS NULL
RETURN s.session_id, s.timestamp
```

**Check whether a user exists before writing to avoid orphaned data** (write)
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})
RETURN u IS NOT NULL AS exists
```

**Delete a test user and everything attached to them** (write, destructive — used by `test_knowledge_graph.py`'s cleanup step; never run against a real `user_id`)
```cypher
MATCH (u:User {user_id: $user_id})
OPTIONAL MATCH (u)-[:HAS_SESSION]->(s:Session)
OPTIONAL MATCH (s)-[:CONTAINS_SCORE]->(sc:Score)
DETACH DELETE u, s, sc
```

